{"obsah":"<p>The date of the event was set last spring, but it was still unclear whether the event could be held this year at all. We knew we were going for a lean solution and adapted the programme accordingly. One of the big concessions was cancelling the riders from England, as it was impossible to predict how the pandemic and the limits on the number of starters would develop.<br>In the end we kept the event in the Tehov park again, thanks also to the support of the municipality and local people, and it turned out to be a good choice. The preparation itself was marked by rain and storms, which complicated mainly the pump track and in the end forced us to cancel the beam and log section for Trial, which we shed a few tears over given all the fine-tuning.</p>\n\n<p><br>We won't beat around the bush. The weather turned out great, over 90 riders came, and thanks to TERRA (JCB), Autosalon BENO Říčany (ŠKODA), the Inplem farm, the Tehov volunteer fire brigade, instructor Klárka Hájková, the guys from Cage Warriors, perfect sound and hosting by Aleš Matoušek and many volunteers, an estimated 500–600 spectators came throughout the day. In the morning they cheered on the Trial riders and the motorbike exhibition by Dalibor Šulc and Tomáš Hůla. Some combined it with a trip from the children's day in Říčany, so the chance to operate a digger, pet the cows or play with the firefighters' equipment was certainly an interesting bonus for all the kids (and, let's be honest, for us parents and riders too).<br>This year Trial was divided into several parts. Unfortunately holidays and injuries weakened our club line-up a bit, and some took on organisational duties rather than the handlebars, but even so the kids' categories filled up beyond expectations. After the kids, the Elite riders took to the course. As it was an exhibition race, everyone rode in one category, so the guys could compare themselves with each other as in the final of a big race. The courses were rideable and set with the weather in mind, but there were a few sharper passages too. Lukáš Valný deserves huge respect – despite being heavily involved in the organisation, he finished third. Matouš Balík's performance was a surprise: although he's a junior by age, thanks to consistent riding he scored just 6 penalty points. The club kids were curious about Vlasta Kabeláč Čiháček's performance, and probably even he didn't know what to expect after 2 years without racing, with 40 on his neck and after his 6th knee operation. A new bike and a relaxed race resulted in 0 penalty points, so there was no contest.</p>\n\n<p><br>The break between the kids' and adults' practice was filled with a small jumping contest, won once again with an exhibition performance by Vlasta, with 120 cm over the tape and a 225 cm jump off a height, ahead of Lukáš Valný, Tomáš Kočička and Matouš Balík.</p>\n\n<p><br>In the afternoon the main roles were played by the boys and girls on the pump track, battling against the clock at a very sharp pace. Lots of kids came to see how much they could get out of themselves. The highlight of the day was the full-suspension race, dominated by the local duo of Lukáš's. Lukáš Turek took first place and also fifth in Experts (hardtails). After the Trial and especially the whole week of preparations, Lukáš Valný had to wake up a bit, but made up for it with 2nd place, becoming the only rider to stand on the podium in all disciplines.</p>\n\n<p><br>The junior category was taken by talented rider Tobík Dolák, who after a very decent Trial performance jumped on a hardtail and won ahead of the winner of one of the kids' Trial categories, Jonáš Vavřinec, and Tommi Neuwirth.<br>The highlight of the event was the Expert category race, with a number of top riders including MTB legend Michal Maroši. Michal suffered a bit after his vaccination, but switched into race mode, grabbed the prize money with first place, including the best jump award, ahead of Alex Sidor and Hugo Novák. Unfortunately there was no shortage of crashes either. The Best Crash award went to Martin Králíček, who luckily only came away with a decent supply of scrapes. Worse was the result of an innocent misstep by Martin Vavřinec, who chose the pump track race over Trial and unfortunately tore his cruciate ligament. We wish him a speedy recovery. The best-placed woman, despite a dislocating shoulder and three kids to look after, was another instructor from the club – Katarína Tóthová.</p>\n\n<p><br>Many thanks to everyone for taking part, helping and supporting. We are donating part of the entry fees to support people affected by the tornado. Unfortunately this also affected several riders who were supposed to come, so hopefully it will help a little. We also thank the municipality of Tehov for supporting the event and lending us the park, and of course the town of Říčany.</p>\n\n<p><br>A video from the event will follow – hopefully see you at the next edition. You can also watch a short report on ČT Déčko (we'll announce the date).</p>\n\n<p><br>The team of the MTB &amp; TRIAL Mraveniště Říčany club and the organisers of Říčanské Šlapačky</p>\n\n<p><br><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2017%2F03%2FResults_TRIAL-a-Pumptrack-2021.pdf?alt=media\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Trial and Pump track 2021 results (PDF)</a></p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped\"><ul class=\"blocks-gallery-grid\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2F205098571_1207400569709899_7725167411954572598_n.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2F205098571_1207400569709899_7725167411954572598_n.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"192634\" data-full-url=\"https://firebase